# Drafted by Gemini (R17 shore), edited.

~ arrive
cutscene mr_moonsong
Narrator: The marsh trail gives out onto wet slate and black reeds, where a lone rowboat knocks against its stake in the rising mist.
cutscene mr_moonsong_2
Narrator: Across the flat grey lake stands the red brick bulk of the sanatorium, its high windows humming with a cold violet glow.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Something large under that water, friends. The reeds lean wrong.
cutscene end
set mr_arrived_shore
if not quest.all_is_well >= the_crossing
quest all_is_well the_crossing
endif
-> END

~ boat
Narrator: The weathered skiff has six damp seats and two heavy ash oars resting in the locks, smelling of tar and lake weed.
* Row to the isle -> row
* [if flag.mr_dredger_carving] Hang the fisher's carving on the prow -> row_carving
* Look around the shore first -> END

~ row
Narrator: Three miles of dead water lie ahead, thick with pale pondweed that trails like wet wool beneath the surface.
* [Survival DC 13] Keep to the clear water -> row_clear | row_dredger
* Row hard and hope -> row_dredger

~ row_clear
Narrator: You read the dark channels between the weed beds and ease the oars through without raising so much as a ripple.
set mr_crossed
move mr_isle:from_boat
-> END

~ row_dredger
cutscene mr_dredger
Narrator: Something vast and pallid turns beneath the keel, and a rotting ribcage of a jaw breaches the water right beside your oars.
cutscene mr_dredger_2
Narrator: Cold lake brine washes over the gunwale before the great shape sinks back into the dark, leaving only greasy bubbles behind.
cutscene end
set mr_dredger_roused
set mr_crossed
move mr_isle:from_boat
-> END

~ row_carving
approve lucan_houndstooth +2 silas_vane +2: You lashed the fisher's carving to the prow to ward off the beast
cutscene mr_dredger
Narrator: A pale bulk rises from the weeds, its crooked maw parting just beneath the driftwood figure lashed to the bow.
cutscene mr_dredger_2
Narrator: Taking one look at its own ugly likeness in the wood, the creature flinches away and slides back into the deep.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Critics are always hardest on their own faces, darling. What a dreadful profile.
cutscene end
set mr_crossed
move mr_isle:from_boat
-> END

~ hut
Narrator: On a workbench inside the leaning shack sits a driftwood carving of a long-jawed, rotting fish-thing, smelling faintly of old tallow.
Narrator: Scratched into the plank beneath it is a warning that the lake beast cannot bear the sight of its own face.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Keen fieldcraft from the fisher. Even a lake beast mislikes a mirror.
set mr_dredger_carving
-> END

~ isle_arrive
cutscene mr_isle
Narrator: Four other rowboats bump softly against the pilings of the wet dock, while fine rain patters on the gravel path above.
cutscene mr_isle_2
Narrator: Before the heavy iron double doors stands a dry stone fountain, crowned with a barn owl that stares down through the mist.
cutscene end
set mr_arrived_isle
if not quest.all_is_well >= sign_in
quest all_is_well sign_in
endif
-> END

~ fountain
Narrator: The dry basin collects only rainwater and dead leaves, though a single tarnished silver coin glints beneath the stone owl's talons.
* Take the coin -> fountain_coin
* Leave it -> END

~ fountain_coin
approve silas_vane +1 rook_coldwake -1: You took the tarnished silver coin from the owl fountain
gold +1
set mr_fountain_coin
Narrator: The coin is cold and slick in your palm, and the carved barn owl above seems to tilt its worn face to watch you pocket it.
-> END
